description:
Analyze the social network graph in the 'demodb' database to find connections between users. Using OrientDB Studio or the API, perform the following tasks:

1. Find the shortest friendship path (bidirectional) from 'john.smith@example.com' to 'thomas.schafer@example.com'.
2. Find the shortest friendship path from 'john.smith@example.com' to 'elena.petrakis@example.com'.
3. Check if a path exists between 'john.smith@example.com' and 'yuki.tanaka@example.com'.
4. List all 'friends of friends' (exactly 2 hops away) for 'john.smith@example.com' (excluding John and his direct friends).

Save your findings to '/home/ga/shortest_path_results.json' in the following JSON format:
{
  "path_to_schafer": {
    "hops": <number>,
    "path_emails": ["email1", "email2", ...]
  },
  "path_to_petrakis": {
    "hops": <number>,
    "path_emails": [...] 
  },
  "path_to_tanaka_exists": <boolean>,
  "friends_of_friends": ["emailA", "emailB", ...]
}

Note: Treat 'HasFriend' edges as bidirectional for this analysis.
